      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "The goal of this study was to examine the incidence of dorsal radiocarpal ligament (DRCL) tears in patients having diagnostic arthroscopy for chronic wrist pain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "A chart review was performed of 64 patients who had diagnostic wrist arthroscopy for chronic wrist pain that was refractory to conservative measures. For each case, interosseous ligament instability/tears were graded according to the Geissler classification. Tears of the triangular fibrocartilage complex and the presence or absence of a DRCL tear were noted."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There were 35 of 64 wrists (in 64 patients) with DRCL tears. The average duration of wrist pain prior to treatment was 20 months. Only 10 patients could recall a specific injury. Five patients had an isolated DRCL tear. A scapholunate interosseous ligament injury was identified in 13 patients, of whom 7 had a concomitant DRCL tear. A lunotriquetral interosseous ligament injury was present in 7 patients, of whom 2 had a concomitant DRCL tear. Two patients had a capitohamate ligament tear: 1 of these patients had a DRCL tear. There were 7 patients with a solitary triangular fibrocartilage complex tear: 6 of 7 were in association with a DRCL tear. One patient had a chronic ulnar styloid nonunion and a DRCL tear. Two or more lesions were present in 23 patients; DRCL tears were present in 12."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "DRCL tears are commonly seen with injuries to the primary wrist stabilizers. Recognition of this condition and further research into treatment methods are needed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "TYPE OF STUDY/LEVEL OF EVIDENCE",
          "content": "Diagnostic IV."
        }
      ]},
